WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.740
- And I know that there's
actually the black trans movement,

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:03.913
as well happening right now, like,

00:00:03.913 --> 00:00:05.981
Black Trans Lives Matter, right?

00:00:05.981 --> 00:00:08.300
- Yeah. Oh yeah it's been
going on for a very long time,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.490
and I think we've just,

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.310
people have started to pay attention,

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.150
and I mean, we have a
long way to go, right,

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.750
like there's unfortunately
in the month of June,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.070
there'd been murders of
several trans people,

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.220
all black trans women,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.500
well except for one,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.370
mostly black trans women this month,

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.990
but also trans women, trans
people of all races and genders.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.270
Tony McDade is a trans
man, he was murdered,

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.510
May 27th, two days after George Floyd,

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.503
in Tallahassee, Florida,
by police officers there.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.340
So it's a movement that's
been going on for a long time,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.270
and there's attention now

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.530
that we're getting to understand now

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.660
when we say Black Lives Matter,

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.760
that has to include all black lives,

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.593
that like,

00:00:47.593 --> 00:00:49.360
just because I'm transgender,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.710
doesn't mean that I'm not
affected by the same racism

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.720
that the rest of the
world is also affected by.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.260
So we're getting there,
we have a long way to go,

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:01.100
in terms of really being
fully inclusive of everyone,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.000
but that's the country,
that's the world, so.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.020
- Yeah. But I think, I don't know,

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.690
do you feel hope with
what's happening right now,

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:08.523
a little bit?

00:01:08.523 --> 00:01:09.490
Sometimes, it depends on the day,

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:10.990
sometimes I feel like overwhelmed,

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.880
and I'm like, we are
never gonna get anywhere.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.870
And then other days, I feel like,

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.978
you hear these stories of like, just hope,

00:01:16.978 --> 00:01:19.650
and people doing the right thing,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.190
and that makes me hopeful.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:22.250
Where are you at?

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.300
- Politicians don't always give me hope,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.400
but the people give me hope.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.117
Seeing, I mean I think after-

00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:29.170
- Well there's more
people than politicians.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.380
- Amen, preach.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.380
So after what happened to George Floyd,

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:35.360
I think that if people
hadn't taken to the streets,

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.360
and hadn't, you know, mobilized,

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.830
then I would really feel
off, I would feel horrible.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:40.930
And I thought, you know,

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.680
after you know, we saw
Mike Brown, and Tamir Rice,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.513
and Trayvon Martin,

00:01:44.513 --> 00:01:46.040
that something would change.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.672
So I have hope because
the people have mobilized,

00:01:48.672 --> 00:01:51.460
and that the people are not relenting,

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.060
and I think we need to not relent,

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.310
and we need to continue
to make our demands,

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.020
and I feel emboldened and inspired

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.240
by everyone out there
marching, so keep marching,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.850
keep protesting peacefully,

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.890
and keep spreading love and awareness,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.313
and keep demanding justice.

